{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/3578-the-crucible-of-fate-discussion-spoilers","id":3578,"title":"The Crucible of Fate Discussion (Spoilers)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T09:56:16-08:00","id":3578,"title":"The Crucible of Fate Discussion (Spoilers)","content":"So I finally got around to reading through the adventure. It's an excellent glimpse of the social side of the Arisen, of course, and highlights the conflict that threatens to split the Su-Menet and general Arisen asunder, which is all very fun. No major spoilers, though we get a snippet of <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> and some insight into how Ammut operates... Personally I'd love to get a <i>lot</i> more information on the Shuankhsen, so the Roller is pretty intriguing especially as it seems like he might be trying to free himself of Ammut as the Heretic freed himself of the Judges... Which means the thing could well end up an absolute mess with loyalist and rogue Shuankhsen, traditionalist, progressive and moderate Arisen and who knows what else... (the Deceived, maybe?). <br /> <br /> Also, it seems the Judges and Ammut herself can make Relics. That's a pretty huge deal, IMO. Bane Relics are an especially nasty idea. There's a lot of mileage in 'em. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm wondering if he traitor is Tashakti or if she's too obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T07:55:09-08:00","id":22336,"title":"","content":"I want to run a Mummy Chronicle. Is there a way to integrate this story with the one shot in the main book, or should I just skip that one and run this as it evolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T08:15:54-08:00","id":22344,"title":"","content":"It offers guidelines to integrate it into an existing story or set up as a new one. With some minor tweaks. I think it works best with using the one-shot in the core book as a prelude, possibly having Hasmut planning his escape to the city where you set your story, thereby bridging both stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T13:46:18-08:00","id":22563,"title":"","content":"So you think that running the one-shot in the core book as a prelude to the main chronicle in the supplements is viable then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T05:09:51-08:00","id":23068,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. Sacmis has one of her jars destroyed in the protagonists' city, so it can drag a meret of Arisen from any location into this chronicle. You could even leave again after part one, if you were so inclined. It works well as either a solo adventure or as part of a greater whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T05:51:54-08:00","id":23086,"title":"","content":"Precisely what GG said. The chronicle can start in Rio de Janairo with the events involving Sacmis &amp; Hasmut (who essentially destroys his cult) then continue (possibly with new characters) in your city of choice. The prelude characters can then become Storyteller NPCs to help guide the story at later points. The nice thing about the Crucible of Fate story is that it draws Arisen from around the world to the Conclave, so conceivably it works really well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T06:35:08-08:00","id":24334,"title":"","content":"I was glad to come across the idea that there are relics attuned to the Devourer. Now my first adventure will have a bit more of a foundation.<br /> <br /> In it, the PC Arisen is awakened by her cult to destroy the Scorpion King (yep, that one) who's supposed to awaken any day now. The Scorpion King's existence, though, isn't bound by an Ammut-twisted Rite of Return; rather, the Devourer forged a relic from his literal beating heart, so the PC must destroy that. Knowing that Ammut can create bane relics helped me fill in some blanks for that plot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T16:10:10-08:00","id":24723,"title":"","content":"Id love if you posted your game stats for the Scorpion King. I've been inspired by the second film to develop it as a possible flashback story set in the eve of the Endless Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T05:34:26-08:00","id":25049,"title":"","content":"That's a really good idea, too! My campaign vision is that the first story is a stand-alone arc, but using a super ancient flashback to describe my canon's Scorpion King's origins would make a very interesting interlude later on, nodding to the early adventures of the PC. Thanks!<br /> <br /> We're getting started WAY later than initially anticipated, but I'm sitting down with my PC to create her Mummy this weekend, after which I'll start the Actual Play thread! When we get to the climactic battle with the Scorpion King I'll definitely post up the stats I used.<br /> <br /> The rough mechanics I have in my head right now, though, are just a shuankhsen with the scorpion stinger merit (and its pre-requisite merits) from <i>Predators</i>, a Werewolf: the Forsaken supplement. He has a bane affinity, Ammut's Feast - which the PC will be cursed with as well, upon destroying the demon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}